{
    "definitions": {
        "eventLoopProbes": "[atMs, delayMs]: a UI-thread timer set to fire every 50 ms; delayMs is how much later it fired. A large delay means the UI thread was busy (or the app was throttled in the background), not that a frame took that long to draw.",
        "frameSwaps": "When each window's QQuickWindow::frameSwapped fired, timed on its render thread. An interval between swaps is not GPU time, compositor latency or when the frame reached the screen. Qt draws only when something changes, so long intervals while idle are normal.",
        "samples": "Every 500 ms: process CPU time as % of one core since the previous sample, resident memory, macOS memory footprint, and thread count. null means the platform didn't provide it."
    },
